        <div id="soil-moisture" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            6. Soil Moisture Decides the Result
          </h2>

          <p>
            If there is one step that separates a lawn that was aerated from one that was merely driven over, it is moisture. Dry clay is close to concrete. Tines skid across it or pull shallow, broken plugs no matter how much weight is on the tray. Saturated soil is the opposite problem: the tines smear the walls of the holes and the plugs turn to paste, and running equipment on a waterlogged lawn compacts it further.
          </p>

          <p>
            What you want is soil that is moist several inches down but not muddy at the surface. The simplest way to get there is to water about an inch the day or two before you aerate, or to aerate a day or two after a good soaking rain. The screwdriver test doubles as a moisture check: if it pushes in easily and comes out clean or only slightly damp, you are in the right range. If it comes out coated in mud, wait.
          </p>

          <p>
            Moisture matters most for tow-behind spoon aerators, which rely on weight and rolling motion rather than an engine driving the tines down. The difference between dry and moist soil can be the difference between half-inch dimples and full 3-inch plugs from the same aerator. It matters for manual corers too, just in a more personal way: on moist soil, the Yard Butler slides in with a firm step; on dry clay, you will be bouncing on the foot bar.
          </p>

          <p>
            Before you water, mark sprinkler heads, shallow irrigation lines, invisible dog fence wire and any buried cable with small flags. Tines will not usually reach utility lines, which are buried deeper, but shallow sprinkler heads are an easy thing to break. Mow the lawn a little shorter than usual beforehand, too, so the tines reach soil instead of pushing through tall grass.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 lg:p-8 my-8">
            <p class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-[#38BDF8] mb-4">AERATION BY THE NUMBERS</p>
